@star brown-dwarf
name: Brown dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: too small to burn hydrogen: the same stuff as a star, cool enough for molecules (water, methane, ammonia) in its air
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
mass-jupiter: 13..80
stage: too light to burn like a true star
color: magenta-red
tags: dim, failed star
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
temp-k: 250..2800
share-of-stars: common

# ── Dead and strange stars ──

@star white-dwarf
name: White dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 99.9%, helium 0.1%
makeup-note: a skin of pure hydrogen a few kilometres thick; beneath it carbon and oxygen about half and half, the ash of its burning, packed to a tonne a teaspoon
surface-kind: white-dwarf
remnant: yes
real: yes
color: white
stage: the leftover core of a star of about one solar mass
tags: small, dense, cooling
radius-sol: 0.008..0.02
temp-k: 4000..40000
share-of-stars: common

@star neutron-star
name: Neutron star
makeup: iron 100%
makeup-note: a crust of iron nuclei in a sea of electrons; deeper, below about a kilometre, nuclei dissolve into neutrons packed shoulder to shoulder
surface-kind: neutron-star
remnant: yes
real: yes
stage: the crushed core left by a supernova
tags: tiny, extremely dense
radius-sol: 0.000014..0.000017
mass-sol: 1.17..2.35
temp-k: 600000..1000000
share-of-stars: rare

@star pulsar
name: Pulsar
makeup: iron 100%
makeup-note: a crust of iron nuclei in a sea of electrons; deeper, neutrons packed shoulder to shoulder; its beams from its magnetic poles
surface-kind: neutron-star
remnant: yes
real: yes
stage: a spinning neutron star sweeping beams through space
tags: spinning, beams, radiation
radius-sol: 0.000014..0.000017
temp-k: 600000..1000000
share-of-stars: rarest

@star magnetar
name: Magnetar
makeup: iron 100%
makeup-note: a crust of iron nuclei in a sea of electrons, its magnetic field a thousand times a pulsar's; deeper, neutrons packed shoulder to shoulder
surface-kind: neutron-star
remnant: yes
real: yes
stage: a neutron star with an enormous magnetic field
tags: magnetic, star-quakes
radius-sol: 0.000014..0.000017
temp-k: 600000..1000000
share-of-stars: rarest

@star black-hole
name: Stellar black hole
surface-kind: normal
real: yes
stage: the collapsed core of a very heavy star
tags: no light, swallows matter
radius-sol: 0.000004..0.00004

@star cepheid
name: Cepheid variable
makeup: hydrogen 91.2%, helium 8.7%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%, sulfur 0.0013%, argon 0.0003%, aluminium 0.0003%, calcium 0.0002%, sodium 0.0002%, nickel 0.00017%
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
stage: a giant that swells and shrinks on a steady beat
tags: pulsing, variable
radius-sol: 20..200
temp-k: 5500..6600
share-of-stars: rarest

# ── Luminosity classes (how bright for its type) ──

@class hypergiant
name: Hypergiant (class 0 / Ia+)
real: yes
says: the brightest, heaviest stars, losing mass in huge winds
example: Eta Carinae

@class supergiant
name: Supergiant (class I)
real: yes
says: enormous, very bright stars near the end of their lives

@class bright-giant
name: Bright giant (class II)
real: yes
says: between giants and supergiants

@class giant
name: Giant (class III)
real: yes
example: Arcturus

@class subgiant
name: Subgiant (class IV)
real: yes
says: a star just starting to swell into a giant

@class main-sequence
name: Main-sequence star (class V)
real: yes
says: a star steadily burning hydrogen, as most stars are

@class subdwarf
name: Subdwarf (class VI)
real: yes
says: dimmer than a main-sequence star of the same color

# ── Extra star types ──

@star carbon-star
name: Carbon star (class C)
makeup: hydrogen 90.5%, helium 9.4%, carbon 0.08%, oxygen 0.045%, nitrogen 0.02%, neon 0.008%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: more carbon than oxygen at its surface, dredged up from its burning shell: soot in its air
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
color: deep red
says: a cool giant whose air is rich in carbon
radius-sol: 100..400
temp-k: 2500..3200
share-of-stars: rarest

@star s-type
name: S-type star
makeup: hydrogen 90.5%, helium 9.4%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.04%, nitrogen 0.02%, neon 0.008%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%, zirconium 0.00002%, barium 0.000003%, technetium 0.0000001%
makeup-note: between an ordinary giant and a carbon star: zirconium, barium and the short-lived technetium freshly made inside it
surface-kind: giant
real: yes
says: a cool giant between ordinary red giants and carbon stars
radius-sol: 100..300
temp-k: 2400..3500
share-of-stars: rarest

@star l-dwarf
name: L-type brown dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: cool enough for dust clouds of iron and silicates in its air
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
says: the warmest brown dwarfs, with metal-hydride clouds
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
temp-k: 1300..2200
share-of-stars: uncommon

@star t-dwarf
name: T-type brown dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: cool enough for methane and water in its air
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
says: cooler brown dwarfs with methane in their air
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
temp-k: 500..1300
