@star y-dwarf
name: Y-type brown dwarf
makeup: hydrogen 91%, helium 8.8%, oxygen 0.045%, carbon 0.025%, neon 0.008%, nitrogen 0.006%, magnesium 0.004%, silicon 0.003%, iron 0.003%
makeup-note: cool enough for ammonia clouds, near room temperature
surface-kind: brown-dwarf
real: yes
says: the coldest brown dwarfs, barely warmer than a planet
radius-sol: 0.08..0.12
temp-k: 250..500
share-of-stars: rare

@star rr-lyrae
name: RR Lyrae variable
makeup: hydrogen 91.5%, helium 8.4%, oxygen 0.02%, carbon 0.008%, neon 0.003%, nitrogen 0.002%, magnesium 0.0015%, silicon 0.001%, iron 0.0005%, sulfur 0.0005%
makeup-note: an old star, poor in the heavier elements (about a tenth of a young star's share)
surface-kind: normal
real: yes
says: an old pulsing star that brightens and dims in less than a day
radius-sol: 4..6
temp-k: 6100..7400
